IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cpp-core`
IMPORT `cp5-e-amount`

-- Tests of sections 77 to 80.1 (cp5-e-amount.l4). Expected values were worked out by hand from the text.

§ `Tests of sections 77 to 80.1`

§§ `Fixtures`

-- A year of one tier, with no division unless the last three fields say so.
GIVEN upe IS A NUMBER
      underAct IS A NUMBER
      underProvince IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `cp5 Year of earnings of one tier`
`cp5 test fixture -- a year without a division` upe underAct underProvince MEANS
    `cp5 Year of earnings of one tier` WITH
        `unadjusted pensionable earnings of the tier for the year` IS upe
        `earnings on which a contribution of the tier has been made for the year under this Act` IS underAct
        `earnings on which a contribution of the tier has been made for the year under a provincial pension plan` IS underProvince
        `the year is a year of a division of unadjusted pensionable earnings` IS FALSE
        `unadjusted pensionable earnings of the tier attributed by the division` IS 0
        `total unadjusted pensionable earnings of the tier for the year determined for the division` IS 0

GIVEN upe IS A NUMBER
      attributed IS A NUMBER
      total IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `cp5 Year of earnings of one tier`
`cp5 test fixture -- a year of a division` upe attributed total MEANS
    `cp5 Year of earnings of one tier` WITH
        `unadjusted pensionable earnings of the tier for the year` IS upe
        `earnings on which a contribution of the tier has been made for the year under this Act` IS 30000
        `earnings on which a contribution of the tier has been made for the year under a provincial pension plan` IS 10000
        `the year is a year of a division of unadjusted pensionable earnings` IS TRUE
        `unadjusted pensionable earnings of the tier attributed by the division` IS attributed
        `total unadjusted pensionable earnings of the tier for the year determined for the division` IS total

§§ `Sections 78 to 78.2`

-- 30000 under this Act and 10000 under a provincial plan: three quarters.
#ASSERT `s 78 — the proportion of a year's base unadjusted pensionable earnings attributable to base contributions made under this Act` 30000 10000 EQUALS JUST 0.75
#ASSERT `s 78.1 — the proportion of a year's first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings attributable to first additional contributions made under this Act` 30000 10000 EQUALS JUST 0.75
#ASSERT `s 78.2 — the proportion of a year's second additional unadjusted pensionable earnings attributable to second additional contributions made under this Act` 30000 10000 EQUALS JUST 0.75
-- Nothing under this Act: nil. Nothing under a provincial plan: all.
#ASSERT `s 78 — the proportion of a year's base unadjusted pensionable earnings attributable to base contributions made under this Act` 0 5000 EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `s 78 — the proportion of a year's base unadjusted pensionable earnings attributable to base contributions made under this Act` 5000 0 EQUALS JUST 1
-- Nothing under either: the divisor is nil, so the text does not decide.
#ASSERT `s 78 — the proportion of a year's base unadjusted pensionable earnings attributable to base contributions made under this Act` 0 0 EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Sections 79 to 79.2`

-- 20000 attributed of a total of 50000: two fifths.
#ASSERT `s 79 — the proportion of a year of a division's base unadjusted pensionable earnings attributable to base contributions made under this Act` 20000 50000 EQUALS JUST 0.4
#ASSERT `s 79.1 — the proportion of a year of a division's first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings attributable to first additional contributions made under this Act` 20000 50000 EQUALS JUST 0.4
#ASSERT `s 79.2 — the proportion of a year of a division's second additional unadjusted pensionable earnings attributable to second additional contributions made under this Act` 20000 50000 EQUALS JUST 0.4
#ASSERT `s 79 — the proportion of a year of a division's base unadjusted pensionable earnings attributable to base contributions made under this Act` 20000 0 EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Which section governs a year, and the total it gives`

-- Not a year of a division: section 78 (three quarters). A year of a division: section 79 (two fifths).
#ASSERT `cp5 helper -- the proportion that applies to a year of one tier` (`cp5 test fixture -- a year without a division` 50000 30000 10000) EQUALS JUST 0.75
#ASSERT `cp5 helper -- the proportion that applies to a year of one tier` (`cp5 test fixture -- a year of a division` 50000 20000 50000) EQUALS JUST 0.4
-- Scaled earnings: 50000 at three quarters is 37500; nil earnings stay nil even when the divisor is nil.
#ASSERT `cp5 helper -- the unadjusted pensionable earnings of a year as scaled by the proportion` (`cp5 test fixture -- a year without a division` 50000 30000 10000) EQUALS JUST 37500
#ASSERT `cp5 helper -- the unadjusted pensionable earnings of a year as scaled by the proportion` (`cp5 test fixture -- a year without a division` 0 0 0) EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `cp5 helper -- the unadjusted pensionable earnings of a year as scaled by the proportion` (`cp5 test fixture -- a year without a division` 100 0 0) EQUALS NOTHING
-- The total: the caller's function (here a sum, standing for sections 50 and 51) applied to the scaled amounts.
-- Year 1: 40000 at three quarters = 30000. Year 2: 20000 with nothing under this Act = 0. Sum 30000.
#ASSERT `s 78 and s 79 — the total pensionable earnings attributable to base contributions made under this Act` (LIST `cp5 test fixture -- a year without a division` 40000 30000 10000, `cp5 test fixture -- a year without a division` 20000 0 20000) (GIVEN scaled YIELD sum scaled) EQUALS JUST 30000
-- Add a year of a division: 40000 at one quarter (10000 attributed of 40000) = 10000. Sum 40000.
#ASSERT `s 78 and s 79 — the total pensionable earnings attributable to base contributions made under this Act` (LIST `cp5 test fixture -- a year without a division` 40000 30000 10000, `cp5 test fixture -- a year without a division` 20000 0 20000, `cp5 test fixture -- a year of a division` 40000 10000 40000) (GIVEN scaled YIELD sum scaled) EQUALS JUST 40000
-- A year with earnings but nothing under either plan: the text does not decide.
#ASSERT `s 78 and s 79 — the total pensionable earnings attributable to base contributions made under this Act` (LIST `cp5 test fixture -- a year without a division` 100 0 0) (GIVEN scaled YIELD sum scaled) EQUALS NOTHING
-- The two additional tiers work the same way (one year, three quarters of 40000).
#ASSERT `s 78.1 and s 79.1 — the total first additional pensionable earnings attributable to first additional contributions made under this Act` (LIST `cp5 test fixture -- a year without a division` 40000 30000 10000) (GIVEN scaled YIELD sum scaled) EQUALS JUST 30000
#ASSERT `s 78.2 and s 79.2 — the total second additional pensionable earnings attributable to second additional contributions made under this Act` (LIST `cp5 test fixture -- a year without a division` 40000 30000 10000) (GIVEN scaled YIELD sum scaled) EQUALS JUST 30000

§§ `Section 77`

-- 30000 of 40000 base: three quarters.
#ASSERT `s 77 — the proportion of a benefit that is payable under this Act` 30000 0 0 40000 0 0 EQUALS JUST 0.75
-- With all three tiers: (30000 + 3000 + 0) / (40000 + 4000 + 1000) = 33000 / 45000 = 11 / 15.
#ASSERT `s 77 — the proportion of a benefit that is payable under this Act` 30000 3000 0 40000 4000 1000 EQUALS JUST (11 DIVIDED BY 15)
-- Everything under this Act: the whole.
#ASSERT `s 77 — the proportion of a benefit that is payable under this Act` 40000 4000 1000 40000 4000 1000 EQUALS JUST 1
-- Nothing at all to divide: the text does not decide.
#ASSERT `s 77 — the proportion of a benefit that is payable under this Act` 0 0 0 0 0 0 EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Section 80`

-- A benefit of 1000 and a proportion of three quarters.
#ASSERT `s 77 and s 80 — the amount of the benefit that is payable under this Act` 1000 (JUST 0.75) `no agreement under section 80 puts the whole of the benefit under one plan` EQUALS JUST 750
#ASSERT `s 77 and s 80 — the amount of the benefit that is payable under this Act` 1000 (JUST 0.75) `an agreement under section 80 puts the whole of the benefit under this Act` EQUALS JUST 1000
#ASSERT `s 77 and s 80 — the amount of the benefit that is payable under this Act` 1000 (JUST 0.75) `an agreement under section 80 puts the whole of the benefit under the provincial pension plan` EQUALS JUST 0
-- Without a proportion, only an agreement decides.
#ASSERT `s 77 and s 80 — the amount of the benefit that is payable under this Act` 1000 NOTHING `no agreement under section 80 puts the whole of the benefit under one plan` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 77 and s 80 — the amount of the benefit that is payable under this Act` 1000 NOTHING `an agreement under section 80 puts the whole of the benefit under this Act` EQUALS JUST 1000

§§ `Section 80.1`

-- Within the limits: 400 under this Act and 300 elsewhere against 600 otherwise payable.
#ASSERT `s 80.1(4) — the agreement is within the limits that subsection (4) sets` FALSE FALSE 400 300 600
-- (c) 200 + 300 = 500 is less than 600.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 80.1(4) — the agreement is within the limits that subsection (4) sets` FALSE FALSE 200 300 600)
-- (c) at the boundary: 300 + 300 = 600 is not less than 600.
#ASSERT `s 80.1(4) — the agreement is within the limits that subsection (4) sets` FALSE FALSE 300 300 600
-- (d) 700 under this Act is greater than the 600 otherwise payable; exactly 600 is not.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 80.1(4) — the agreement is within the limits that subsection (4) sets` FALSE FALSE 700 0 600)
#ASSERT `s 80.1(4) — the agreement is within the limits that subsection (4) sets` FALSE FALSE 600 0 600
-- (a) and (b).
#ASSERT NOT (`s 80.1(4) — the agreement is within the limits that subsection (4) sets` TRUE FALSE 400 300 600)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 80.1(4) — the agreement is within the limits that subsection (4) sets` FALSE TRUE 400 300 600)
-- Subsection (3): an agreement applies, within the limits: the agreement's amount.
#ASSERT `s 80.1(3) — the disability benefit payable under this Act for the month` TRUE TRUE 400 600 EQUALS JUST 400
-- No agreement: the amount otherwise payable.
#ASSERT `s 80.1(3) — the disability benefit payable under this Act for the month` FALSE TRUE 400 600 EQUALS JUST 600
-- An agreement outside the limits: the text does not say what is payable.
#ASSERT `s 80.1(3) — the disability benefit payable under this Act for the month` TRUE FALSE 700 600 EQUALS NOTHING
